@startuml domain-usage
title warren/domain — identity, aggregates, events, specifications\nsource: warren.md §3.1 (implemented; spec retired 2026-08-01); warren.md §3.1

participant "aggregate constructor\nNewUser(...)" as ctor
participant "User\n{ AggregateRoot[UserID] }" as agg
participant "Repository[*User, UserID]\n(port, T Root[K])" as repo
participant "persistence.UnitOfWork\n[context — §3.3]" as uow

== Construction — identity before the first event ==
ctor -> agg : AggregateRoot:\ndomain.NewAggregateRoot(NewUserID())
ctor -> agg : Raise(UserRegistered{...})
note right of agg : Raise records, publishes NOTHING —\nevents wait for the unit of work
note right of agg : Entity[T].ID() is the identity accessor;\nID constraint = comparable + fmt.Stringer

== The generic seam ==
note over agg, repo : Root[K] is the constraint repositories are generic over:\n  ID() K + PullEvents() []Event\nAggregateRoot satisfies it — a struct cannot be a Go type\nconstraint, so this interface makes Repository[T Root[K], K ID]\nexpressible (compiler-verified 2026-08-01)

== Save — the only place events leave ==
repo -> agg : load / save *User
uow -> agg : PullEvents() — drains and clears,\ninside the business transaction
uow -> uow : store aggregate + outbox\nin ONE transaction (§5.5)

== Specification — one predicate, two uses ==
ctor -> repo : FindBy(ActiveUsers())
repo -> repo : spec.ToSQL() → clause + args\n(a repository MAY translate)
ctor -> ctor : spec.IsSatisfiedBy(user)\n— same rule, in memory
@enduml
